<div class="lp-note"><strong>Run a small campaign before buying a year.</strong><p>Test authentication, contact handling, reply assignment, exports and suppression of people who opt out. Choose the workflow your team can run consistently.</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="lp-section" id="calling"><div class="lp-wrap">
{{ g.heading('05','Give the campaign a calling plan','How cold calling can support<br>Instantly or Smartlead campaigns.','A useful call can confirm the right contact, uncover a timing issue or move a conversation forward when email has stalled.') }}
<div class="sg-flow"><div><h3>Choose accounts worth calling.</h3><p>Use company fit, role and a clear reason to speak. An email open alone is a weak reason to move someone to the top of the list.</p></div><div><h3>Use the context naturally.</h3><p>Say why you called and ask a useful question. If an email is relevant, mention it briefly. Do not make the prospect search for it before explaining the point.</p></div><div><h3>Keep one clear next step.</h3><p>Record the result, respect stop requests and assign follow-up. Pause or adjust the email sequence when a conversation changes the plan.</p></div></div>
<p class="dg-related">Prepare with our <a href="/resources/cold-call-scripts/">free cold calling scripts</a>, compare <a href="/resources/best-cold-calling-dialers/">cold calling dialers</a>, or use the <a href="/resources/best-crm-for-outbound-sales/">outbound CRM guide</a> to organise follow-up.</p>
</div></section>
